# OPERATOR STATE. `make pi-ship` does not overwrite the copy on the Pi
# (PI_OWNED in the Makefile). git holds only the seed for a fresh
# install. Edit on the Pi: `sudo pf tui`, Agent lists, then apply.
pi-fortress-block.test

# The full product of each destination below is "accept data from
# anyone and hand it back anywhere". They have no place on a home
# network. A block on them costs nothing that anyone will miss.
#
# This list, not allow.domains, is the durable half of the fence.
#
# The agent segment is already deny-by-default. Thus for the agent, these
# are a second layer. But blocklists run before the allow oracle and
# still win (corepolicy.Forward.Allowed). Thus a sink stays closed even
# if someone in a hurry widens allow.domains later.
#
# The house segment is the real reason that they are here. house.domains
# and house_default.domains are sinkholes, not allow lists: a laptop or a
# phone on the house may reach all names that are not on one. For the
# house, this list is the full fence.
#
# To un-block, name the domain in never_block.domains. Never delete the
# line here.

# --- out-of-band / webhook catchers: an agent's C2 rendezvous of choice
webhook.site
requestbin.com
pipedream.net
beeceptor.com
requestcatcher.com
hookbin.com
mockbin.org
interact.sh
oast.fun
oast.pro
oast.live
oast.site
oast.online
oast.me
burpcollaborator.net
dnslog.cn
ceye.io

# --- anonymous paste: text out, no account, no trace
pastebin.com
hastebin.com
dpaste.com
dpaste.org
termbin.com
paste.ee
controlc.com
rentry.co
justpaste.it
telegra.ph

# --- anonymous file drops: the same, for bytes
transfer.sh
file.io
bashupload.com
oshi.at
gofile.io
catbox.moe
uguu.se
anonfiles.com
tmpfiles.org
0x0.st

# --- reverse tunnels: turn any box on either segment into an ingress
ngrok.com
ngrok.io
ngrok-free.app
ngrok.app
trycloudflare.com
localtunnel.me
loca.lt
serveo.net
pagekite.me

# --- dynamic DNS: a name that moves is a name a fence cannot reason about
duckdns.org
no-ip.com
ddns.net
dynu.com
hopto.org
zapto.org
